<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Washington Naval Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Washington Naval Treaty was an arms-limitation agreement signed in February 1922 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the United Kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-naval-conference">Washington Naval Conference</a>. It fixed ratios for the tonnage of capital ships, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the United States parity, halted battleship building for ten years, and lapsed after Japan withdrew in the 1930s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/washington-naval-treaty.jpg" alt="Washington Naval Treaty" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington_Naval_Treaty.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
